question 8) Multi-level Inheritance
class A {
    void show() {
        System.out.print("A ");
    }
}

class B extends A {
    void show() {
        System.out.print("B ");
    }
}

class C extends B {

}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        A obj = new C();
        obj.show();
    }
}
==========================================output==================================================


C doesn't override show().

It inherits B.show().

Dynamic dispatch finds nearest override.

Output:

B
